"""The cffi declarations of ``sdk/libzxv/include/zxv_api.h`` (ABI 1.6).

This is the ONE place the SDK describes the C ABI. ``tests/test_cdef_drift.py``
parses the header and fails if any ``ZXV_API`` function is missing here or
has a different signature, so the two cannot drift apart silently.

The declarations are copied from the header with comments removed. Enum
typedefs are not needed: every function takes plain ``int32_t`` for them.
Constants live in :mod:`zxv._constants` as Python integers.
"""

